WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.470
A urine sample holds thousands
of different chemicals,

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.860
including breakdown products
of drugs and hormones.

3
00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.910
Early in a pregnancy, one more joins them:

4
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.920
a hormone called hCG, made by the embryo.

5
00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:19.850
A strip of paper, dipped in the sample,
finds that one hormone among all the rest.

6
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.210
How can a paper strip pick out one
hormone from the thousands of chemicals in

7
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:25.880
a urine sample?

8
00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:29.460
In this mission, you'll
meet monoclonal antibodies:

9
00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:33.780
identical antibodies, all
made by one clone of cells.

10
00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.560
Then you'll follow the
urine along a test strip,

11
00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:39.380
past a test line and a control line.

12
00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:44.490
Your mission: explain how a paper strip
picks out one hormone from thousands of

13
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.870
chemicals in urine.
